{{was wotd|2009|October|30}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|morbidus||diseased}}, from {{m|la|morbus||sickness}}, itself from the root of {{m|la|morior||die}} or directly from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*mor-||to rub, pound, wear away}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɔː.bɪd/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɔɹ.bɪd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-morbid.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{label|en|originally}} Of, or relating to [[disease]].
# Taking an interest in [[unhealthy]] or [[unwholesome]] subjects such as [[death]], [[decay]], [[disease]].
# Suggesting the [[horror]] of [[death]]; [[macabre]] or [[ghoulish]]
# [[grisly|Grisly]] or [[gruesome]].

====Derived terms====
* [[morbidity]]
* [[morbidly]]
* [[morbidness]]

====Related terms====
